# Copy to `.env` and adjust. `.env` is git-ignored; this file is not.
#
# pydantic-settings matches these names to the fields on `Settings` in
# app/config.py case-insensitively, so DATABASE_URL populates
# `database_url`. Every variable listed as REQUIRED below has no default
# — the app raises a ValidationError at import time if it's missing,
# which is deliberate: a missing config value should fail loudly at
# startup, not silently at the first request that needs it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local Postgres from docker-compose.yml at the repo root.
#
# Two things about this URL that are easy to get wrong:
#
#   1. The `+asyncpg` suffix picks SQLAlchemy's async driver. Without
#      it, SQLAlchemy defaults to the sync psycopg driver and
#      create_async_engine() fails.
#
#   2. Do NOT append `?sslmode=require` or `?channel_binding=require`.
#      Those are libpq/psycopg parameter names; SQLAlchemy passes URL
#      query params straight through to asyncpg's connect(), which
#      doesn't recognize either one and raises a TypeError rather than
#      ignoring them. This bites specifically when copying a connection
#      string out of Neon's dashboard, which generates both by default.
#      See docs/dev/notes.md for the full write-up.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/calendar_dev

# The Ollama model tag the agent worker extracts with. `gemma4:e4b` is
# the outcome of the model evaluation in docs/dev/env-setup.md Phase 5 —
# not a default, an actual decision. Confirm it's pulled with
# `ollama list` before running the worker.
# gemma4:e4b alone runs at Ollama's 4096-token default window (its /v1 endpoint ignores a
# request's num_ctx), which truncates long pages. Use the derived model instead — see
# apps/api/ollama/gemma4-e4b-32k.Modelfile and docs/dev/notes.md.
MODEL_NAME=gemma4-e4b-32k

# Where the worker's model calls go. There is no default in the code: this variable is the only place the URL
# comes from, and the worker refuses to start without it (agent_worker.main.model_endpoint_problem). Here it is
# the local Ollama's OpenAI-compatible endpoint. A hosted run overrides it on the command line (see below); a hosted
# worker sets it in its service variables. The API never calls a model and leaves it unset.
MODEL_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHERE THE MODEL CALLS GO — C6
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# The URL is MODEL_BASE_URL above; the rest default to the local Ollama's needs. One endpoint serves every call site
# (the page model, the act splitter, the status question, reconcile's artist matcher); a role can have its own
# MODEL NAME, not its own URL or key (c6-hosted-inference.md, C6-D2).
#
# For a HOSTED run (DeepInfra) put only the KEY here, so it never lands in shell history or a chat, and pass the
# rest as a one-command override, so `make worker` on the laptop never silently becomes a paid run:
#   MODEL_BASE_URL=https://api.deepinfra.com/v1/openai MODEL_PROVIDER=openai_compatible \
#     MODEL_NAME=google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it uv run python -m agent_worker.model_eval.run_eval --label ...
# MODEL_API_KEY=
# Per-role model names (each falls back to MODEL_NAME when unset or empty):
# SPLITTER_MODEL_NAME=
# STATUS_MODEL_NAME=
# MATCHER_MODEL_NAME=

# Optional. A larger model for the third (last) retry attempt of a failed extraction
# (arch-initial.md §7; agent_worker/policy.py). Leave unset on a laptop that can't run one:
# attempt 3 then reruns MODEL_NAME with the full retry hint, and the attempt record says so.
# ESCALATION_MODEL_NAME=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHICH ENVIRONMENT THIS PROCESS IS — C3
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# One of local | dev | staging | prod. Optional, and `local` when unset, which is right for a laptop. A hosted
# service sets it, and the app REFUSES TO START when it disagrees with where the process really is (app/config.py,
# C3-D4): a local value with a hosted database, a hosted value with a local one, a database login role that does
# not end in the environment (calendar_staging), a Railway environment of another name, or (for a HOSTED MongoDB
# only; a local one is skipped) a MongoDB database of another name, so a hosted override also sets MONGODB_DATABASE. The point is that a wrong connection string stops the process instead of writing to the wrong place.
#
# CONSEQUENCE for the one-command override that reaches a hosted database from the laptop: it must NAME its
# target, so the check can see the intent. Never edit this file to point at a hosted database.
#   APP_ENV=prod DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://calendar_prod:...@<neon host>/neondb uv run alembic upgrade head
# APP_ENV=local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# AGENT WORKER (`make worker`) — A4
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the worker stages each extraction attempt's raw record before validation judges it
# (arch-initial.md Section 6; docs/dev/implementations/a4-auditability.md, A4-D3). Locally this is the
# `mongo` service in docker-compose.yml (`make db-up`). The worker refuses to start without it: an
# audit trail that silently skips its raw record isn't auditable. The API doesn't need it. Atlas
# (hosted) is C3's (the databases) and C8's (the worker) in alpha-deployment-plan.md.
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017
# MONGODB_DATABASE=calendar

# How the worker's log lines render: `auto` (default) is readable text on a terminal and JSON
# otherwise; force one with `console` or `json`. See app/log_config.py.
# LOG_FORMAT=auto

# Feature flags (FLAG_*) are NOT set here. A flag's value comes from the process environment only, and
# `Settings` refuses a FLAG_* line in this file at startup. Set one on the command that reads it, for example
# `FLAG_WORKER_SCHEDULED_RUNS=true make worker`. See docs/dev/environments.md, "Feature flags".

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# TEST VARIABLES — shell / CI environment ONLY. Do NOT put these in .env.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# TEST_DATABASE_URL  Overrides where the DB tests run. Default: DATABASE_URL
#                    with the database name swapped to `calendar_test`, and
#                    only if its host is local. The test fixtures DROP and
#                    recreate that database, so the name must be exactly
#                    `calendar_test`.
# REQUIRE_DB=1       Turn "Postgres isn't reachable" from a skip into a
#                    failure. `make test` / `make check` set it; so does CI.
# MONGODB_TEST_URI   Where the one real-MongoDB test (agent_worker/tests/
#                    test_staging_mongo.py) connects. Default
#                    mongodb://localhost:27017. It skips when nothing answers
#                    there, except under CI, where it fails instead.
#
# Why not in .env: `Settings` (app/config.py) forbids unknown keys, so an
# extra line here raises a ValidationError for the whole app, Alembic and
# every test — and pydantic-settings doesn't export .env values to
# os.environ anyway, so the test fixtures would never see them.
#   TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/calendar_test pytest

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT YET REQUIRED — listed so the shape is known before it's needed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# MongoDB Atlas, the hosted form of MONGODB_URI above. The cluster is already
# provisioned (env-setup.md Phase 7); pointing the worker at it is milestone C8 (C3 creates the databases).
# MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://<user>:<password>@<cluster>/?retryWrites=true&w=majority

# Cloudflare R2, for per-page snapshots from the Fetch step. Deferred —
# see alpha-build-plan.md section 8. audit_log.snapshot_key stays null
# until this exists.
# R2_ENDPOINT_URL=
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# R2_BUCKET=

# Shared secret for the Next.js -> FastAPI server-to-server call
# (arch-initial.md Section 5). Deferred: no FastAPI dependency checks
# it and no fetch call sends it yet, so setting it now would be an
# unused value.
# API_SHARED_SECRET=
